# Local tests before GitHub push

Do not `git push`, `gh pr create`, or otherwise publish to GitHub until the full Playwright suite has passed **three consecutive times** locally after the latest change.

## Required sequence

```bash
npx playwright test
npx playwright test
npx playwright test
```

All three runs must exit 0. Use the repo’s configured projects (do not drop browsers or use `--last-failed` as a substitute).

## Reset the count

- If any run fails, fix the failure, then start over at run 1.
- If you change specs, page objects, config, or fixtures after a passing streak, start over.

## Do not

```bash
# ❌ BAD — one green run, then push
npx playwright test && git push

# ❌ BAD — skip browsers or reuse a failed-only rerun
npx playwright test --project=chromium
git push
```

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — three full-suite passes, then push
npx playwright test
npx playwright test
npx playwright test
git push
```
